Description: libevdev.pc requires linux-input-shim
 The installed libevdev/libevdev.h and libevdev/libevdev-uinput.h include
 <linux/input.h> and <linux/uinput.h>. NextBSD has no /usr/include/linux:
 nextbsd-displayserver-support's linux-input-shim installs those two headers
 (each an #include of the base kernel's <dev/evdev/...> header) in
 /usr/include/linux-input-shim and adds that directory through its own
 linux-input-shim.pc. Requiring it here makes `pkgconf --cflags libevdev`
 enough to compile against the installed headers. libevdev's own build uses
 the copy in its include/linux/freebsd and is unchanged.
Origin: NextBSD (nextbsd/nextbsd-displayserver-support#1, E25)
Forwarded: not-needed
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -91,6 +91,7 @@
 	version: meson.project_version(),
 	libraries: lib_libevdev,
 	subdirs: 'libevdev-1.0',
+	requires: 'linux-input-shim',
 )
 
 man_config = configuration_data()
